{
  "name": "Krayin CRM pipeline",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Krayin CRM pipeline\n\n### How it works\n\nThis workflow is a callable Krayin CRM pipeline processor that prepares CRM reference data, checks for an existing contact, then checks for matching leads. Depending on the conditions, it creates a missing contact, updates an existing lead, retrieves product information, and either creates or updates a lead in the appropriate pipeline stage. The layout flows left to right from the workflow trigger through lookup, decision, and final lead write operations.\n\n### Setup steps\n\n- Configure the Krayin credentials on all Krayin nodes so they can access the correct CRM instance.\n- Ensure the calling workflow passes the fields needed for contact lookup, lead lookup, product retrieval, and lead creation or update.\n- Review the IF node conditions to confirm they match your CRM rules for detecting existing contacts, leads, and products.\n- Verify the pipeline, stage, product, contact, and lead field mappings in the Krayin nodes before enabling the workflow.\n\n### Customization\n\nAdjust the IF conditions and Krayin node mappings to match your sales process, such as using different identifiers for contacts/leads or routing new leads to different pipelines and stages.",
        "height": 880,
        "width": 480
      },
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -64,
        -176
      ],
      "id": "4df297fc-44b0-4e4a-a6b9-31c8481da4af",
      "name": "Sticky Note"
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Start and CRM lookup\n\nReceives the execution from another workflow and loads Krayin pipeline, stage, and contact data needed for the later decisions.",
